{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788370832,"nonce":"OsRrvKFqDSujVXeF8ssv3fcnowU=","message":"**The naming half is fixed. The wipe-recovery half (comment #1) is untouched and this issue stays open for it.**\n\nShipped: `dialog-accept`, plus an automatic sweep in the advance loop. Dorian's call was to accept the generated name now and file choosing separately — `35a84f6` — on efficiency grounds: the wedge is what blocks an unattended run, and the name the colony ends up with is not.\n\n## What the source says, and it is worse than the issue stated\n\n`RimWorld/Faction.FactionTick`:\n\n    if (Find.TickManager.TicksGame % 1000 == 200 \u0026\u0026 IsPlayer)\n    { ... Find.WindowStack.Add(new Dialog_NamePlayerFactionAndSettlement(settlement)); }\n\nThe 1,000-tick period in the issue is exactly this. The branch is chosen by `NamePlayerFactionAndSettlementUtility.CanNameFactionNow()` / `CanNameSettlementNow(x)`, and those test `!Faction.OfPlayer.HasName` and `!factionBase.namedByPlayer` against 4.3 days elapsed, plus `CanNameAnythingNow()` (a player home map is current, \u003e= 2 spawned free colonists, no active threat, `!GameEnder.gameEnding`). **Nothing in that predicate is about the window** — so this was never a dialog that could be dismissed, and there are FOUR of these windows, not one: `Dialog_NamePlayerFaction`, `Dialog_NamePlayerSettlement`, `Dialog_NamePlayerFactionAndSettlement`, `Dialog_NamePlayerGravship`, all `Dialog_GiveName`.\n\n## Items 1-4 and 6\n\n1. **`dialog-accept {window?, all?}`** — `Source/AutoRimmer/NameDialogs.cs`. Reproduces `Dialog_GiveName.DoWindowContents`' OK branch: `IsValidName` then `IsValidSecondName`, then `Named`/`NamedSecond`, then `TryRemove(doCloseSound:false)`. Reproduced and not called because that method's FIRST statement is `if (Event.current.type == EventType.KeyDown ...)` and `Event.current` is null outside OnGUI — invoking it from `GameComponentUpdate` NREs before it reaches anything. `Messages.Message` dropped as presentation (`historical:false`); `Event.current.Use()` dropped. Every member is `protected` on `Dialog_GiveName`, so the route is reflection bound once and tolerantly, off the BASE declarations — all four are abstract/virtual, so one binding dispatches to every subclass.\n\n   **The widget gate is not waived**, unlike `dialog-dismiss` (DESIGN waiver 2): both validators run in the widget's own order before anything is named.\n\n2. **Supplying text is REFUSED, not ignored** — `VerbArgs.RefuseStray(V, {window, all}, ...)`. A caller that thinks it chose a name and silently got the generated one is the same defect class as item 3. Filed as `35a84f6`.\n\n3. **`dialog-dismiss` no longer claims a bare success on one.** Dismissing a `Dialog_GiveName` now carries `answered:false`, `re_raises_in_ticks:1000` and a warning naming `Faction.FactionTick` and pointing at `dialog-accept`. It still dismisses — the esc-equivalent has to always work — but the envelope no longer says \"handled\".\n\n4. **The wedge does not reach the halt at all.** `TimeDriver.SweepNameDialogs` runs per frame in `Step()`, before the `haltFlag` check and before the force-pause poll, and only when something is already force-pausing. It accepts every open naming dialog, journals `dialog_answered {via:\"auto\", accepted:[...], still_blocking}`, and clears a halt ONLY when `haltReason == \"dialog\"` and the sweep left nothing force-pausing — a naming dialog stacked under a real decision still halts on the real decision. Failure cap of 3 per session, then it gives up with a journal warning and the halt stands; a run should never see a naming halt, and if it does, the `gate` says why. `config.json`'s `autoAnswerNameDialogs:false` restores the old behaviour.\n\n   This is the mod acting unprompted and it is argued rather than assumed, in `DESIGN.md`'s decisions log: it is the one window the agent structurally cannot answer, because nothing in the protocol writes a text field and the alternative is that no unattended run passes day 4.3.\n\n6. `checklists/triggered.md` gains `colony-naming` (never dismiss; the general lesson is that a section closing before its work falls due hides that work forever). `playbook/PLAY-LOOP.md`'s dialog rule gains the case, with the shape stated generally: **a dialog raised by a periodic predicate is not cleared by closing the window.**\n\nAlso: `interactions` and the `force_pause` halt payload both report these as `kind:\"name-entry\"` with `current`/`second_current`/`uses_second_name` and `answer_with:\"dialog-accept\"`. The issue's own observation — that `interactions` could see the answer and the action surface had no matching write — is closed in both directions.\n\n## One thing found that the issue did not have\n\n`RimWorld/Dialog_NamePlayerGravship` assigns `curName` INSIDE `if (ModLister.CheckOdyssey(\"Grav engines\"))`. Without Odyssey the window opens with `curName == null` and **vanilla's own OK branch throws** on `s.Length` inside `IsValidName`. Refused here as `gate:\"no-current-value\"` rather than reproduced faithfully.\n\n## Still open on this issue — items 7, 8, 9\n\n`Dialog_ChooseNewWanderers` is untouched. It is not a `Dialog_GiveName`; comment #1's scrape shows it carries nothing actionable in its fields, so `dialog-accept` cannot address it and the wipe-recovery path is still terminal. Item 8's broader rule — dismissal that DESTROYS an offer must refuse or warn — is honoured for naming dialogs only, which is the case that can be detected by type today. Item 9 (`PLAY-LOOP.md`'s post-wipe branch) is not written.\n\nNot bench-verified: the DLL is built and the bench is down. Acceptance is the two-command check — raise the dialog via `Verse/DebugActionsMisc`' own action (line 471 constructs one directly), assert `interactions.force_pause.count` goes to 0 and STAYS 0 across a 60,000-tick advance, which is 60 chances for `FactionTick` to raise it again.","files":null}]}